## Build Complete

**File:** `CustomerEscalationSolution/CustomerEscalationFlow/CustomerEscalationFlow.flow`

### What was built

A 10-node Maestro Flow that triggers on every new email in your Outlook 365 inbox and routes it via two-stage classification:

| Node | Type | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `emailReceived1` | Outlook 365 trigger | Fires on new inbox email |
| `classifyEmail1` | Script | Keyword scan (urgent) + domain/address check (VIP) |
| `checkUrgent1` | Decision | Routes on `isUrgent` flag |
| `checkVip1` | Decision | Routes on `isVip` flag (urgent path only) |
| `notifySlackVipEscalation1` | Slack connector | Posts to `#vip-escalations` channel |
| `replyAcknowledgment1` | Outlook 365 connector | Sends VIP acknowledgment reply |
| `doneVipEscalation` | End | Terminal — VIP escalation path |
| `createSupportTicket1` | Freshdesk connector | Creates support ticket |
| `replyWithTicketDetails1` | Outlook 365 connector | Replies with ticket ID and link |
| `doneTicketCreated` | End | Terminal — standard ticket path |

**Routing logic:**
- Urgent **AND** VIP → Slack alert + acknowledgment reply → done
- Urgent only, VIP only, or neither → Freshdesk ticket + ticket-details reply → done

### Validate result

`Status: Valid` — 0 errors, 1 informational warning (intentional: trigger + both reply nodes share the same Outlook 365 connection because they're all using the same mailbox account).

### Before deploying — two things you need to update

1. **Slack channel ID** — `notifySlackVipEscalation1` is configured with placeholder `#vip-escalations`. Open the flow and replace it with your real Slack channel ID (the `C...` style ID, not the display name). You can get it from Slack → right-click the channel → Copy link.

2. **VIP list** — the classifier uses placeholder domains (`vip-client.com`, `bigaccount.com`, `enterprise.com`) and addresses (`ceo@example.com`, `vip@example.com`). Edit the `classifyEmail1` script node and replace those with your actual VIP senders.

